.el .ds Aq '
.TH mdmc 1  "mdmc 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
mdmc \- Markdown mail compiler — compile markdown drafts to RFC 5322 email
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmdmc\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Markdown mail compiler — compile markdown drafts to RFC 5322 email
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config.toml (default ~/.config/mdmc/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mdmc\-new(1)
Create a new email draft
.TP
mdmc\-edit(1)
Open a draft in $EDITOR
.TP
mdmc\-compile(1)
Compile a draft to a message (RFC 5322)
.TP
mdmc\-decompile(1)
Decompile a message to a markdown snapshot note
.TP
mdmc\-reconcile(1)
Mark drafts sent when their message\-id is in the account\*(Aqs sent maildir
.TP
mdmc\-pick(1)
Pick a draft, snapshot, message, or address (interactive)
.TP
mdmc\-list(1)
List drafts, snapshots, messages, or addresses to stdout
.TP
mdmc\-view(1)
Print a message as markdown to stdout (no attachment extraction)
.TP
mdmc\-config(1)
Print the effective (merged, resolved) config as TOML
.TP
mdmc\-index(1)
Build (or rebuild) the lookup index from notmuch
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
